<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86028" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πότῐμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πότος, πίνω</span>) mostly of water, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>drinkable, fresh,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Heraclit.
				61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Medic.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				3.2.19
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρήνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					34.9.5
				</span></i>
			: generally, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Od.</u>
					65
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>fresh, sweet, pleasant,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρποὶ γλυκεῖς καὶ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>CP</u>
					4.4.12
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. λόγος,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλμυρὰ ἀκοή,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				243d
			</span></i>; of the writings of <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.200S.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lib.</u>
				p.46O.
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δόγματα, ἔννοιαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.275
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1.72
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ χρηστὰ καὶ π.,</span> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δυσχερῆ καὶ μοχθηρά,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.469c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> of persons,
				<i>pleasant, sociable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				29.31
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); so also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτιμώτερον συμπόσιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					3.10
				</span></i>
			. Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφῶς καὶ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					1.8.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>porous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					947d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>watered, irrigated,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πείσεα.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δευτερίας</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.6.15
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
